Z||000003||bHooper||03-07-2000||09:11 AM||||Yes that is a very nice car!! I am jealous!<P>But I have to ask... why, and how do you plan to do a ttop conversion to a sunroof car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> The car is fine as it is.  If you cut what's left of the roof, will it not make it the body week on the car?   I would hate to see you destroy the car (purely by accident) with the car flexing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Big O||03-07-2000||09:30 AM||||That is without question the most beautiful Fiero GT I've ever seen.  It has just the right level of mods to make it look distinctive and not trashy. (What tire wheel combination are you running?  Those look like Pirelli P4000s).  It makes me want to get out the checkbook and spend the family fortune to bring mine up to the same level.  After all, a good Fierophile would be happy to subsist on bread and water for the rest of his days for a chance to call a car like that his own.  A great big Hoooahh to you!||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||03-07-2000||09:33 AM||||That's some nice tasteful customization, all right.  Love the wheels and the chromed plenum, valve covers and air cleaner box.||||reg||14
