Z||000014||BAM-BAM||03-07-2000||10:02 PM||||  Hey Earne, <P>     That's what I'm talking about; moderate<BR>COOL!. I've seen so many  people who do to much to their vehicles and they look trashy.<BR>You did just enough to enhance the true look of you car and the T-Tops will cap it off nicely. To all  who  read my post(OK MOTORHEADS)that's what I am talking about; keep it calm, keep it classy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I do have one question about the, Sunrooof to T-Top conversion. Are they going to add a center support section to decrease body sag? Just a thought in response to one of the earlier responses you recieved. Take care and beutiful job, first class.<P>  Be Cool, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000015||mrfiero||03-08-2000||01:20 AM||||Just FYI on the T-Tops.....you don't have to reinforce anything when installing them.  The kit he has is identical to the "factory" installed T-Tops on the '88 Fiero.  The frame cutting that is required is minimal and the roof, when installed, will be just as strong as before.  Will there be some minor flexing problems?  Possibly, but not enough to warrant any subframe reinforcement. <P>If this set-up passed GM's standards without any reinforcement, then I would say it is unnecessary.  You must figure that GM tested this thing out before putting their "seal of approval" on it. Considering they would be liable if anything went wrong they certainly would have made sure the integrity of the car was maintained.  <P>I have owned 5 T-Top Fieros and never experienced any troubles, aside from the occasional leak.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000016||Standard||03-08-2000||03:47 AM||||double wow!  very nice car!  normally I don't really like chromed stuff, but the plenum just looks beautiful chromed!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000017||Earne||03-08-2000||07:37 AM||||Has this site been down?  I couldn't connect at all yesterday.<P>SCCA Fiero- Thanks for the comment.<P>DJRice- a lot, 'bout $15-1800.<P>bHooper- The section the tops occupy is bigger than the sunroof.  The frame (center rail) that comes with the kit replaces the rigidity of the side rails.  Yes the car is nice but T-tops are rare, attractive, and they are a great way to get the feeling of ragtop and still keep the GT appearance that makes this car.<P>Big O- Right, on the Pirellis.  The wheels are 17" Primax.  I modified the center caps and the center caps of GT wheels so I could put them together.  They look like they were made with Fiero center caps now.  I'm very fortunate to have a couple bucks to do the work and a wife that approves.  <P>ChadMan- Thanks, by the way, someone asked about a 1987 plenum on a 1986, it works.<P>Raydar- Plenum is chromed.  The only polished pieces are the dogbone and the EGR valve top.  I just saw that PaulV is selling original styled but chromed dogbones.  Think I'll be doing business with him again.<P>SCCA Fiero-  You're right.  The chroming is the cheap part.  Stripping, and polishing are the labor intensive jobs.  Yes, you have to polish the plenum first to get it to come out like that.  I worked with Nolan Bishop when he first got he Fiero business going, paid less.  The list price today is $600 with a core.  He takes yours and give you a new one.  No down time.<P>Ferrari355- THANKS!  The car only took second in the All Pontaic show last fall.  The competition is TUFF around here (Michigan).<P>mutfish-  Thanks, nice of guys like you to notice.<P>Monkeyman- Yes, will that be cash or check?<P>rcn491- Thanks, PISA, just found the bill 'cause someone else asked, $600.<P>BAM-BAM- Thanks, yes the center support is part of the kit.<P>mrfiero- Thanks, well put.<P>Standard- Thanks, the best part is that all this stuff is bolt on if Ed Parks does my 3.4 upgrade.  Everything fits perfectly.  The only diff is performance.<P>I hope you guys read this, I really appreciate having people who know what they are talking about make these comments.  By the way, anyone wanting to talk to Nolan Bishop call (419) 385-1708.  He has a lot of parts for sale and he made the custom shock tower covers.  If anyone asks I will mail his brochure to you.  Another by the way, no one mentioned the side scoops.  I wasn't satisfied with anyone's so I made them myself.  Like Mechams but without the strakes.  Like the Pontiac design but the fill the entire panel instead of the upper section.  Phil at FOCOA saw them last year (pic on page 19 of the latest FOCOA mag) and now he is selling the Fiero 2000 scoop.  Maybe I need to talk design fees with Phil.  Again, sorry for not getting back right away, I just couldn't get the site to come up.||||reg||12
