Z||000022||Earne||03-09-2000||01:19 AM||||theogre- I was hoping nobody asked that question.  I went on one of my walks through the automotive recycling center (junk yard) and found this near full size black Pontiac probably around a '92-'94.  Pontiac has used the same or similar components through the years on different models.  Anyway, there it was, on the underside of the hood, riveted to one of the braces.  I have a lot of great things that way but I don't always remember the donor car.  My Fiero club gets on my case about it.  I also installed an auto dimming mirror with a digital compass from some '97-'99 Cadilac, as well as power mirrors from another Fiero.  Sorry I couldn't be more specific.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Cliff Pennock||03-09-2000||05:05 AM||||Earne, the site wasn't down but for some reason my site and your ISP couldn't reach each other. I was getting a lot of returned emails from my server because it couldn't send you the email notification for this topic. I also replied to your email you had sent me, but that was returned also. Maybe your ISP had an over-active firewall or something and it has been corrected since.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Earne||03-09-2000||06:42 AM||||Thanks for responding Cliff, I have had a lot of trouble with my ISP, Concentric.  It takes a little while around here (up to 30 days to install) but I have just signed up with AT&T for a cable modem.  I'm believe my internet activity will be greatly enhanced and hopefully, all the problems will go away.||||reg||1
